pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nBluetooth audio from a phone or laptop to this computer's speakers: bluetooth_audio_status says who is playing and how. bluetooth_audio_connect connects a paired phone for audio, bluetooth_audio_disconnect ends it, bluetooth_audio_pairing lets a new phone pair for two minutes (each asks the person); the person compares the number on the phone and on Settings -> Bluetooth themselves. The volume of the phone's sound is the sound source named after the phone in the speaker settings. The other direction: bluetooth_audio_send_status says whether sound is going to headphones or a speaker, bluetooth_audio_send_start sends this computer's sound to a paired pair of headphones or a speaker (SBC only, each asks the person), bluetooth_audio_send_stop ends it, bluetooth_audio_send_tone plays a two second test tone to them (asks). bluetooth_audio_send_start sends ALL of this computer's sound to them and by default silences its own speakers (mute_speakers=false keeps them on; whole_computer=false only connects). Say plainly that sending was tested against a fake speaker only, not with real headphones, and that the speakers play again at once when the stream stops or fails.";
